WEBVTT

00:02.500 --> 00:03.920
(Student Council Office)

00:05.880 --> 00:07.710
We're back.

00:08.130 --> 00:10.880
Welcome back. Thank you...

00:11.300 --> 00:12.220
Well,

00:12.300 --> 00:13.760
you're holding something amazing.

00:14.260 --> 00:15.720
Isn't it cute?

00:15.800 --> 00:17.680
It's cute,

00:17.970 --> 00:20.640
but you're not thinking
of putting it here, are you?

00:21.560 --> 00:22.810
Can I?

00:23.190 --> 00:25.900
No. Please give me a break.

00:28.270 --> 00:30.030
These are the supplies we bought.

00:30.110 --> 00:31.110
Let's see.

00:32.320 --> 00:33.990
It's just the usual supplies.

00:34.360 --> 00:36.070
Kuze, you're a great help.

00:36.160 --> 00:39.280
If Kujou had gone alone,
I don't know what would've happened.

00:40.950 --> 00:44.290
The student council office
would've turned into a dreamland.

00:46.750 --> 00:47.960
What do you think, Kuze?

00:48.040 --> 00:50.300
You still don't want
to join the student council?

00:50.380 --> 00:51.300
Well,

00:51.380 --> 00:53.670
I don't mind helping out once in a while.

00:54.090 --> 00:55.010
In that case,

00:55.090 --> 00:58.140
shouldn't you at least put
your name on the member list?

00:58.970 --> 01:00.810
Do you also agree, Kujou?

01:01.180 --> 01:03.100
No, putting my name...

01:03.560 --> 01:04.480
Come to think of it,

01:04.560 --> 01:06.230
I can understand if it's Yuki,

01:06.310 --> 01:08.980
but President,
why do you want me to join so badly?

01:10.360 --> 01:13.610
Why do you not want
to join the student council?

01:13.690 --> 01:16.950
I don't think hard work
is the only reason.

01:17.570 --> 01:18.620
Because I'm not

01:18.700 --> 01:21.700
cut out to be a member
of the student council.

01:22.290 --> 01:25.370
But I think otherwise.

01:25.750 --> 01:26.870
After all,

01:26.960 --> 01:28.330
didn't you accomplish a lot

01:28.420 --> 01:31.710
as an outstanding vice president
of the junior high student council?

01:32.090 --> 01:34.590
I know I'm not a good fit
precisely because of that.

01:35.050 --> 01:36.180
After all,

01:36.260 --> 01:39.720
I didn't fight for that position
for some grand purpose.

01:42.390 --> 01:44.100
What's wrong with that?

01:44.350 --> 01:45.180
What?

01:45.480 --> 01:46.600
You know what?

01:46.690 --> 01:50.610
I became the president
to get the girl I like.

01:50.980 --> 01:54.480
Isn't this motive more impure than yours?

01:58.450 --> 01:59.700
Is that so?

02:00.990 --> 02:02.410
Look at this.

02:03.580 --> 02:05.410
Is this your younger brother?

02:05.870 --> 02:07.790
This is when I was in ninth grade.

02:11.170 --> 02:12.130
What?

03:33.630 --> 03:35.500
(Alya Sometimes Hides Her Feelings in Russian)

03:43.970 --> 03:45.800
(Episode 4: Overflowing Emotions)
Are you surprised?

03:45.890 --> 03:47.180
(Episode 4: Overflowing Emotions)
Yes.

03:47.560 --> 03:49.980
(Episode 4: Overflowing Emotions)
How should I put it? You've changed a lot.

03:50.390 --> 03:53.190
Two years ago, I was just as you saw.

03:53.270 --> 03:54.520
My grades were terrible.

03:54.610 --> 03:55.900
I was bad at sports too.

03:56.150 --> 03:59.690
To be honest, I didn't even like school.

04:00.190 --> 04:02.200
But even though
we weren't compatible at all,

04:02.280 --> 04:04.700
I fell in love
with one of the two beauties

04:04.780 --> 04:06.370
in the same grade.

04:06.990 --> 04:09.450
Do you mean your girlfriend, President?

04:09.660 --> 04:11.580
Yes. The current vice president,

04:11.660 --> 04:13.120
Chisaki Sarashina.

04:13.870 --> 04:17.040
In order to become a man worthy of her,

04:17.130 --> 04:18.710
I went all out to change myself.

04:19.090 --> 04:22.590
Taking over the presidency
was also part of my plan.

04:23.470 --> 04:24.470
What do you think?

04:24.550 --> 04:25.470
Is it impure enough?

04:27.050 --> 04:28.640
Indeed, it is.

04:28.970 --> 04:30.060
That's why

04:30.140 --> 04:32.390
things like motives don't matter.

04:32.770 --> 04:34.520
Including Kujou over there,

04:34.600 --> 04:37.810
she joined the student council
only because Chisaki invited her.

04:37.900 --> 04:39.020
Is that so?

04:39.400 --> 04:40.530
That's right.

04:40.780 --> 04:44.530
Well, I was interested
in the student council too.

04:45.320 --> 04:46.280
I think

04:46.370 --> 04:47.910
no matter what your motive is,

04:47.990 --> 04:51.250
it's okay as long as you
leave behind a good track record.

04:51.660 --> 04:53.750
Whether the cause is love or friendship,

04:53.830 --> 04:55.080
as a student council member,

04:55.170 --> 04:58.250
as long as you organize
various activities well for students,

04:58.340 --> 04:59.170
it'll be fine.

04:59.670 --> 05:01.170
Is that so?

05:01.920 --> 05:02.840
Yes.

05:03.130 --> 05:04.010
Otherwise,

05:04.090 --> 05:08.510
only saints can be politicians.

05:09.300 --> 05:11.810
Well... that's true.

05:12.220 --> 05:13.600
That's right.

05:13.850 --> 05:15.690
When you were in junior high school,

05:15.770 --> 05:18.900
as the vice president,
you did achieve a lot with Suou.

05:19.400 --> 05:21.190
It's nothing to be ashamed of

05:21.280 --> 05:23.990
or guilty about.

05:25.650 --> 05:27.490
(Seiren Academy Junior High School
Student Council Office)

05:28.160 --> 05:29.200
Masachika.

05:29.490 --> 05:31.540
Stay by my side forever.

05:32.080 --> 05:34.200
No way. It's too much of a hassle.

05:34.290 --> 05:37.210
Hey, aren't you my brother?

05:40.210 --> 05:43.800
Joining the student council
to make someone the president

05:44.170 --> 05:45.590
is the best thing you can do.

05:46.180 --> 05:49.010
Me, Chisaki, and Kujou all welcome you.

05:49.680 --> 05:51.510
No one will criticize you.

05:53.100 --> 05:55.100
I'll think about it.

05:55.680 --> 05:57.020
Think about it carefully.

05:57.100 --> 05:59.520
Worrying is the privilege of the young.

05:59.770 --> 06:02.400
You're still young too, President.

06:02.480 --> 06:03.320
To be honest,

06:03.400 --> 06:05.820
you don't look like a sophomore at all.

06:06.990 --> 06:08.030
I get that a lot.

06:08.490 --> 06:11.490
I was mistaken
for a graduate student the other day.

06:11.870 --> 06:15.540
- To make someone the president?
- Well, you do look dignified.

06:15.620 --> 06:16.540
You think so?

06:16.620 --> 06:18.620
Hey, where's Alya?

06:20.040 --> 06:23.090
She went to settle a dispute
between the baseball and soccer clubs.

06:23.460 --> 06:24.550
Dispute?

06:25.090 --> 06:26.090
During this period,

06:26.170 --> 06:29.130
the baseball club
uses the field frequently to prepare

06:29.220 --> 06:31.010
for the annual inter-school competition.

06:31.090 --> 06:34.310
But this year, the soccer club
is joining the regional preliminaries.

06:34.600 --> 06:38.140
So they want the baseball club
to give up the right to use the field.

06:38.520 --> 06:41.310
So Alya went to mediate for that?

06:41.770 --> 06:42.610
Yes.

06:42.690 --> 06:44.820
Neither of them wants to give in.

06:45.110 --> 06:48.030
It seems scouts will come
to recruit from the baseball club.

06:48.400 --> 06:49.610
Come to think of it,

06:49.700 --> 06:52.700
I saw the captain
of the baseball club on TV that day.

06:53.200 --> 06:56.120
As the hope of the baseball club,
he's pretty famous.

06:56.580 --> 07:00.420
Chisaki is usually in charge
of club disputes like this.

07:00.500 --> 07:03.380
But she's busy with the kendo club today.

07:03.790 --> 07:08.010
I thought it would be a good experience,
so I sent Alya.

07:08.090 --> 07:10.510
But I guess it's not that easy.

07:11.800 --> 07:13.720
Well, I'll be going now.

07:13.850 --> 07:14.810
(Student Council Office)

07:16.470 --> 07:18.430
I'm just going to check

07:18.520 --> 07:19.890
if they're fighting.

07:29.070 --> 07:29.900
I told you.

07:29.990 --> 07:32.530
It's better to practice soccer
on home ground.

07:32.610 --> 07:33.990
It's no use saying that.

07:34.070 --> 07:35.990
We've been doing this every year.

07:36.080 --> 07:38.200
The venue was booked a long time ago.

07:38.290 --> 07:39.330
That kind of game

07:39.410 --> 07:41.420
is just like a friendly match, right?

07:41.500 --> 07:42.580
No, it's not!

07:42.790 --> 07:44.000
Please calm down.

07:44.080 --> 07:45.630
Criticizing each other like this

07:45.710 --> 07:46.710
is pointless.

07:46.960 --> 07:48.960
Well, do you have any alternatives?

07:49.460 --> 07:51.300
Why don't we use the riverbank nearby

07:51.380 --> 07:54.340
as an alternative practice field?

07:54.430 --> 07:56.350
What? Riverbank?

07:58.060 --> 08:00.430
Isn't there a baseball field
by the riverbank?

08:00.520 --> 08:01.640
It's decided then.

08:01.730 --> 08:02.730
Are you kidding me?

08:02.810 --> 08:04.610
Isn't there a soccer field too?

08:04.690 --> 08:07.320
But the school field's
conditions are better.

08:07.400 --> 08:08.980
We think so too!

08:09.070 --> 08:12.240
It's an important game
that will affect our future!

08:12.320 --> 08:14.570
Don't just think about yourself!

08:14.660 --> 08:15.990
Besides,

08:16.070 --> 08:19.120
the soccer club has more members than you.

08:19.200 --> 08:22.210
Considering the travel time,
you guys should go.

08:22.290 --> 08:24.920
- Stop. Please calm down.
- Don't give me that nonsense!

08:25.000 --> 08:27.090
- No one
- Our future...

08:27.170 --> 08:29.710
- will listen to me.
- We need to practice soon.

08:30.510 --> 08:31.720
I...

08:32.300 --> 08:35.590
can't move people's hearts.

08:40.180 --> 08:41.390
If this is the outcome

08:41.770 --> 08:44.020
of having expectations for someone,

08:44.480 --> 08:46.400
I'll just do it alone.

08:47.360 --> 08:48.320
No one

08:48.400 --> 08:51.110
will follow me anyway.

08:54.490 --> 08:56.740
It's my fault for always
looking down on others,

08:56.820 --> 08:57.990
pushing them away,

08:58.080 --> 09:00.330
and refusing to get close to anyone.

09:00.870 --> 09:02.620
This is the price I have to pay.

09:03.580 --> 09:08.210
Who would listen to someone like this?

09:08.880 --> 09:12.300
Someone like me
who's always so condescending

09:12.380 --> 09:13.800
and speaks about big truths.

09:15.470 --> 09:16.590
I'm always

09:17.090 --> 09:18.220
alone.

09:19.100 --> 09:20.220
I get it.

09:20.600 --> 09:21.640
I get all that.

09:22.270 --> 09:24.730
It's my own choice.

09:24.980 --> 09:26.020
But...

09:26.690 --> 09:27.690
But...

09:30.150 --> 09:31.280
Help me.

09:33.110 --> 09:34.240
Someone,

09:35.110 --> 09:36.360
please help me.

09:39.580 --> 09:40.910
Hello.

09:43.500 --> 09:45.910
Sorry to interrupt your discussion.

09:46.000 --> 09:48.040
I'm from the student council.

09:49.170 --> 09:50.710
I'm the general affairs officer,

09:50.790 --> 09:52.300
Masachika Kuze.

09:56.220 --> 09:59.220
It's an important game
that will affect our future!

09:59.300 --> 10:01.640
(Soccer Club)
Don't just think about yourself!

10:01.720 --> 10:02.930
Besides,

10:03.020 --> 10:06.100
the soccer club has more members than you.

10:06.190 --> 10:09.310
Considering the travel time,
you guys should go.

10:09.520 --> 10:12.020
Stop. Please calm down.

10:13.780 --> 10:16.200
It's no use saying that now, Alya.

10:16.990 --> 10:19.700
Both sides are fuming.

10:20.410 --> 10:22.740
It'd be better
to start the discussion anew.

10:23.660 --> 10:25.290
Well, I feel sorry for you,

10:25.370 --> 10:26.910
but it's an experience.

10:27.580 --> 10:29.330
Do your best, Alya.

10:29.880 --> 10:30.920
Help me.

10:33.130 --> 10:34.460
Someone,

10:35.170 --> 10:36.420
please help me.

10:40.180 --> 10:42.220
That's why you're always alone.

10:42.720 --> 10:45.060
Crying for help in a way
that no one understands.

10:46.390 --> 10:47.310
All right.

10:48.060 --> 10:48.890
I got it.

10:52.190 --> 10:53.400
Kuze?

10:53.980 --> 10:55.230
Kuze?

10:55.320 --> 10:58.030
The Kuze who was
the vice president in junior high?

10:59.200 --> 11:02.030
I've been briefed by the president.

11:02.280 --> 11:04.540
Are you arguing over

11:04.620 --> 11:08.120
the distribution of the school field
and the riverbank practice field?

11:08.710 --> 11:10.210
Yes, that's right.

11:10.500 --> 11:11.920
Thank you for your cooperation.

11:12.500 --> 11:14.420
Well then, how about this?

11:14.750 --> 11:16.800
Considering the number of people moving,

11:16.880 --> 11:19.420
we'll have the baseball club
practice by the riverbank.

11:19.880 --> 11:20.800
But in exchange,

11:20.880 --> 11:22.640
the soccer club, which has more people,

11:22.720 --> 11:26.010
will send someone
to the baseball club for support.

11:26.100 --> 11:28.520
Support? What do you mean?

11:28.600 --> 11:32.150
Why are we the only ones
being pushed to the riverbank?

11:32.230 --> 11:33.230
That's right.

11:33.310 --> 11:34.690
And we have a lot of equipment.

11:34.770 --> 11:36.360
- Please calm down.
- I won't allow it.

11:36.440 --> 11:38.280
Because we have more people.

11:38.360 --> 11:40.320
This is tiring.

11:40.400 --> 11:41.910
But we have a lot of equipment.

11:42.160 --> 11:43.070
Well,

11:43.160 --> 11:44.580
if that's the case,

11:44.660 --> 11:47.830
let us managers support the baseball club.

11:48.290 --> 11:49.290
Is that okay?

11:51.290 --> 11:53.420
If it can settle the dispute.

11:55.290 --> 11:56.420
All right.

11:56.500 --> 11:58.340
If the soccer managers
are willing to come,

11:58.420 --> 11:59.920
that would be helpful.

12:00.420 --> 12:01.800
That's right.

12:02.970 --> 12:05.390
They were complaining just now.

12:05.470 --> 12:07.970
They gave us the right to use the field.

12:08.060 --> 12:09.890
Just be patient with this small issue.

12:10.180 --> 12:12.100
All right, I guess we have no choice.

12:13.980 --> 12:16.610
We will accept this condition.

12:16.690 --> 12:17.650
What about you?

12:18.480 --> 12:19.530
Okay.

12:21.700 --> 12:23.820
All right, it's decided then.

12:24.200 --> 12:25.530
Please come

12:25.620 --> 12:29.200
to the student council office tomorrow
and fill out the application form.

12:44.470 --> 12:45.590
I'm sorry.

12:46.800 --> 12:49.390
I interfered in your mediation just now.

12:50.060 --> 12:52.180
I embarrassed you, didn't I?

12:54.190 --> 12:55.190
Not really.

12:55.980 --> 12:58.400
Why did you propose that plan?

12:59.440 --> 13:01.780
Logically speaking,

13:01.860 --> 13:04.450
the baseball club
wouldn't accept such a proposal.

13:04.990 --> 13:05.990
From what I can see,

13:06.070 --> 13:10.990
it seemed like you knew
that the manager would say yes.

13:12.290 --> 13:13.580
Impressive that you noticed.

13:13.660 --> 13:14.790
Of course, I could tell.

13:14.870 --> 13:17.500
Because when the baseball club
was protesting,

13:17.580 --> 13:20.500
you were staring at that senior.

13:23.260 --> 13:25.130
Actually, that senior

13:25.760 --> 13:28.390
is dating the captain
of the baseball club.

13:29.600 --> 13:30.430
What?

13:30.760 --> 13:32.770
So, you didn't know.

13:32.850 --> 13:36.140
The baseball club's hope
and the beautiful manager are a couple.

13:36.480 --> 13:39.110
When they confirmed their relationship,

13:39.190 --> 13:41.530
it caused quite a stir.

13:41.610 --> 13:42.480
I see.

13:43.150 --> 13:44.570
The baseball club's captain

13:44.650 --> 13:47.280
didn't say anything
during the discussion, did he?

13:47.660 --> 13:49.490
He was concerned about his girlfriend.

13:49.580 --> 13:52.040
But from his view,
he can't mix business and pleasure.

13:52.580 --> 13:54.790
On the other hand, the girlfriend

13:54.870 --> 13:56.460
felt awkward because she knew that

13:56.540 --> 13:58.290
the soccer club was being unreasonable.

13:58.880 --> 14:01.300
That's why I knew
that if I proposed that plan,

14:01.380 --> 14:03.210
she would definitely go with it.

14:03.760 --> 14:06.510
In other words, it's a godsend?

14:06.590 --> 14:08.340
That's how it is for them.

14:08.760 --> 14:10.100
But

14:10.180 --> 14:12.470
the baseball club
will naturally feel happy

14:12.560 --> 14:14.810
with the cute girls
supporting their practice.

14:14.890 --> 14:15.930
The soccer club

14:16.020 --> 14:18.190
will also feel happy
for monopolizing the field.

14:18.690 --> 14:19.730
And those two

14:19.810 --> 14:22.730
can overcome club barriers
and go on dates during practice.

14:23.360 --> 14:25.530
It's practically a win-win situation.

14:29.780 --> 14:30.620
President?

14:32.160 --> 14:34.490
Did the negotiation go well?

14:34.870 --> 14:35.910
Yes.

14:36.000 --> 14:37.710
It's all thanks to Kuze.

14:38.960 --> 14:42.380
I see. Well done, Alya.

14:43.170 --> 14:45.210
Is it all according to your plan?

14:46.470 --> 14:48.380
There's no such thing.

14:48.470 --> 14:49.680
The instant you didn't ask,

14:49.760 --> 14:50.890
"What do you mean?"

14:50.970 --> 14:53.310
To some extent,
it was clear you did it on purpose.

14:53.390 --> 14:55.720
Well, you got me.

14:59.190 --> 15:00.400
So, how was it?

15:00.690 --> 15:02.230
Have you made up your mind?

15:02.480 --> 15:03.860
Yes, kind of.

15:04.980 --> 15:07.030
My name is Masachika Kuze.

15:07.110 --> 15:11.570
I would like to become
a member of the student council.

15:11.990 --> 15:13.530
I look forward to working with you.

15:15.870 --> 15:16.910
Without further ado,

15:17.000 --> 15:18.830
please come with me to the office.

15:22.080 --> 15:25.960
I can't help but feel like I've fallen
right into the president's trap.

15:26.050 --> 15:28.880
What goes around comes around, I guess.

15:29.880 --> 15:31.390
It's getting late.

15:31.470 --> 15:34.300
Let's get the proper paperwork tomorrow.

15:34.850 --> 15:36.390
Does it mean if we have time,

15:36.470 --> 15:38.930
he'll ask me to fill out
and submit the form today?

15:39.560 --> 15:40.390
Excuse me.

15:40.480 --> 15:42.100
What's the matter?

15:46.610 --> 15:48.860
Are you really going
to join the student council?

15:48.940 --> 15:49.900
Yes.

15:50.490 --> 15:51.910
Is it...

15:52.110 --> 15:56.030
so you can join the student council
president election with Suou?

15:56.950 --> 15:58.040
What if I say yes?

15:58.540 --> 15:59.870
What will you do then?

16:00.290 --> 16:02.250
Will you give up on running for president?

16:02.620 --> 16:03.580
No.

16:04.130 --> 16:07.000
I'm going to become
the student council president.

16:07.460 --> 16:08.300
Even if

16:08.380 --> 16:09.800
you're my opponent,

16:10.470 --> 16:12.380
I will never give up.

16:15.760 --> 16:17.100
That's true.

16:18.270 --> 16:20.560
After all, you're always like this.

16:20.640 --> 16:21.890
Moving forward bravely.

16:24.060 --> 16:25.190
I see.

16:26.230 --> 16:27.070
Then,

16:27.150 --> 16:29.570
I'll help you become
the student council president.

16:29.650 --> 16:30.530
What?

16:30.990 --> 16:32.150
If you want,

16:32.240 --> 16:34.620
I'll do my best to help you
get elected as president.

16:34.990 --> 16:36.620
I won't let you be alone anymore.

16:37.700 --> 16:38.790
From now on,

16:38.870 --> 16:40.910
I'll support you by your side.

16:42.080 --> 16:43.000
So...

16:46.750 --> 16:48.710
Shut up and take my hand,

16:48.800 --> 16:49.670
Alya!

17:09.070 --> 17:11.280
I'll be in your care from now on, Alya.

17:12.860 --> 17:13.900
Thank you.

17:14.860 --> 17:16.620
I like you.

17:20.830 --> 17:24.080
What's going on?

17:26.750 --> 17:29.880
Come up here, Maschaka.

17:32.970 --> 17:33.920
Seriously?

17:34.260 --> 17:37.220
So I still feel this way?

17:41.640 --> 17:42.980
It hurts!

17:43.060 --> 17:44.310
Why did you squeeze me?

17:44.390 --> 17:45.230
Were you

17:45.310 --> 17:47.310
thinking about another woman just now?

17:48.060 --> 17:49.520
How did you know?

17:51.440 --> 17:53.190
Oh no!

17:53.280 --> 17:56.070
Isn't thinking about a woman from the past
at confession events

17:56.150 --> 18:00.160
the number two thing
a rom-com protagonist should never do?!

18:00.280 --> 18:01.830
(Number One:
Asking "What did you just say?")

18:03.160 --> 18:04.000
Hey.

18:04.080 --> 18:05.000
Yes?

18:05.580 --> 18:06.580
Earlier,

18:06.670 --> 18:09.880
you said you'd support me
from now on, right?

18:10.750 --> 18:13.510
Yes, I did say that.

18:14.050 --> 18:15.510
So after you said that,

18:15.590 --> 18:18.180
were you secretly thinking about Suou?

18:18.260 --> 18:19.890
No, I wasn't thinking about Yuki.

18:20.890 --> 18:23.180
Hey, that really hurt!

18:23.560 --> 18:24.430
Kuze!

18:24.520 --> 18:25.430
Yes?

18:25.730 --> 18:27.230
If you want me to forgive you,

18:27.310 --> 18:29.690
just accept this slap!

18:36.860 --> 18:38.200
Nice slap.

18:38.490 --> 18:39.360
Idiot.

18:47.160 --> 18:48.290
Let's go home.

18:48.710 --> 18:49.630
Okay.

18:52.290 --> 18:53.210
Goodness.

18:53.460 --> 18:56.220
This is the first time
I've been slapped by a girl.

18:56.590 --> 19:00.010
My experience as a man
has further increased.

19:00.090 --> 19:02.890
Did you hit your head when you fell?

19:02.970 --> 19:05.520
There's nothing abnormal with my brain.

19:05.600 --> 19:06.430
That's right.

19:06.520 --> 19:08.690
You don't have
a proper brain to begin with.

19:09.060 --> 19:11.940
What are you saying to a genius,

19:12.020 --> 19:13.480
who was once called a prodigy?

19:13.900 --> 19:14.980
A prodigy?

19:17.280 --> 19:19.070
You don't look convinced at all.

19:23.080 --> 19:24.790
How's your cheek?

19:24.870 --> 19:26.540
Do you need a cold compress?

19:26.620 --> 19:28.580
No, I'm fine.

19:28.960 --> 19:31.210
I can't feel my left cheek though.

19:31.330 --> 19:33.540
That means you're not okay, right?

19:33.750 --> 19:36.300
No, I'm just kidding.

19:36.760 --> 19:38.720
It's just a little numb.

19:39.880 --> 19:40.880
Is that so?

19:43.550 --> 19:44.470
What?

19:47.270 --> 19:49.060
Why are you spacing out?

19:49.140 --> 19:50.890
It's just a cheek kiss.

19:51.350 --> 19:54.270
Isn't that a touch of cheeks?

19:54.360 --> 19:55.320
That's right.

19:55.570 --> 19:56.820
No, but...

19:57.780 --> 19:59.110
The way it felt just now...

19:59.440 --> 20:00.610
No, which one was it?

20:01.150 --> 20:03.160
Well, see you tomorrow.

20:04.660 --> 20:05.990
See you tomorrow.

20:10.910 --> 20:11.790
What?

20:12.040 --> 20:13.080
Just now.

20:13.170 --> 20:14.790
Which one was it?

20:15.250 --> 20:16.710
Alya!

20:16.800 --> 20:20.300
Please tell me the answer in Russian!

21:32.330 --> 21:34.160
I like you.

21:34.870 --> 21:35.710
Like?

21:36.000 --> 21:36.880
Like, as in...

21:36.960 --> 21:39.000
What? As in liking Kuze?

21:39.090 --> 21:40.710
Me?

21:41.380 --> 21:42.460
No!

21:42.550 --> 21:44.680
No!

21:44.840 --> 21:45.680
No way!

21:45.760 --> 21:47.390
That's impossible!

21:49.470 --> 21:52.470
I don't like Kuze.

21:52.560 --> 21:56.730
That was just me getting
carried away by the atmosphere.

21:56.810 --> 21:57.900
That's all.

21:58.940 --> 22:00.270
Suppose it's true,

22:00.570 --> 22:01.400
one step,

22:01.480 --> 22:03.610
no, taking many steps back,

22:03.690 --> 22:05.700
even if I do like Kuze,

22:06.070 --> 22:07.490
I have something

22:07.570 --> 22:09.200
more important to do right now.

22:09.660 --> 22:11.830
That is to become
the student council president.

22:11.910 --> 22:13.200
What I should do

22:13.290 --> 22:15.290
is live up to that expectation.

22:16.000 --> 22:17.420
If I put this matter aside

22:17.500 --> 22:19.590
and confess to him...

22:20.590 --> 22:22.000
What? You like me?

22:22.340 --> 22:23.880
I'm sorry.

22:23.960 --> 22:28.220
That's not what I meant
when I said I'd "support" you.

22:31.350 --> 22:32.180
I

22:32.260 --> 22:33.100
actually

22:33.180 --> 22:34.520
don't like

22:34.600 --> 22:36.390
you either!

22:41.400 --> 22:42.690
I'm home.

22:43.070 --> 22:45.110
Welcome home, Masha.

22:47.280 --> 22:48.200
Masha.

22:48.280 --> 22:49.530
Did something happen?

22:49.820 --> 22:51.370
What? What do you mean?

22:51.660 --> 22:53.200
You're asking me that?

22:56.080 --> 22:57.790
Yes, something good did happen.

22:57.870 --> 23:00.330
I had a wonderful encounter.

23:00.420 --> 23:01.250
What?

23:02.090 --> 23:03.210
Look!

23:03.340 --> 23:04.590
This is Alya Kitty.

23:04.880 --> 23:07.670
Alya Kitty?

23:07.760 --> 23:08.630
Look.

23:08.720 --> 23:10.510
Don't you think she looks like you?

23:10.590 --> 23:12.010
How so?

23:12.260 --> 23:13.810
Like her eyes?

23:13.890 --> 23:14.810
Her eyes or whatnot,

23:14.890 --> 23:16.230
I'm nothing like her, right?

23:16.310 --> 23:17.390
What?

23:19.770 --> 23:21.270
By the way, Alya.

23:21.480 --> 23:23.400
About Kuze...

23:23.900 --> 23:24.730
What is it?

23:25.730 --> 23:26.690
Nothing.

23:26.780 --> 23:28.610
I just think he's a good boy.

23:28.950 --> 23:31.490
I can see why you've fallen for him.

23:31.570 --> 23:34.120
I told you, I don't like him.

23:34.200 --> 23:35.290
Really?

23:35.370 --> 23:36.620
You're so annoying.

23:40.870 --> 23:42.080
I see.

23:42.460 --> 23:44.000
I get it.

23:44.090 --> 23:46.800
You're cute even when you're not honest.

23:47.210 --> 23:48.380
What?

23:49.090 --> 23:52.930
But if you like him,
you should tell him as soon as possible.

23:53.180 --> 23:55.600
It'll be too late
if someone else snatches him away.

23:55.680 --> 23:58.430
What are you talking about?

23:59.690 --> 24:01.400
Youth.

24:06.070 --> 24:07.690
Goodness.

24:08.110 --> 24:09.280
What was that?
